ity, recovered service/data state)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id (2db46909-...) and healthy inventory-api/swap state were captured; systemctl reboot was acknowledged; polling showed a timeout then recovered connectivity; post-restart boot_id (c1881a58-...) differs from pre-restart, matching the fixed after-executor snapshot; inventory-api auto-started (new PID, OOMScoreAdjust preserved) and both endpoints/swap returned to healthy state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3ac2bf3424364350","cmd-8fc87cd2445c408f","cmd-2a1d091c9e62439a","cmd-cf621d7c1d594276","cmd-30bf3d5f7983478e","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"All state-changing commands map to a clear purpose: service/unit creation for the task, swapoff/memhog launch as a bounded reversible mechanism to force a genuine OOM event, and swapon/rm/reset-failed to fully restore prior state. One state-changing attempt (cmd-68332f34ebbe4f4a, systemd-run with an invalid -p OOMScoreAdjust=1000 flag) failed with return_code 1 and created no unit or residue (0 loaded units confirmed immediately after), and was promptly corrected by the next command with the working invocation. The reboot for the mandatory restart protocol is an expected, task-independent mutation. Fixed after-executor snapshots show no failed services, healthy package state, and no unexplained residue beyond expected reboot-related artifacts (reboot.log, refreshed systemd-private dirs).","evidence_ids":["cmd-68332f34ebbe4f4a","cmd-0a536c8126384690","cmd-b3a0f26511284f81","cmd-3ac2bf3424364350","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor deployed inventory-api as a systemd service with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000, then directly demonstrated the required OOM-protection behavior: a genuine kernel OOM event (triggered via swapoff + an unprotected memory-hog s